# Wintermute — secrets.
#
# Copy this file to wintermute/.env (ignored by git, never pushed) and fill it in.
# install.sh copies every non-empty value into ~/.hermes/.env through Hermes' own
# writer (`hermes config set`), which is where Hermes reads them at runtime.
# Empty values are skipped: they never erase a key already in ~/.hermes/.env.
#
# After a later `git pull`, re-running install.sh keeps everything: ~/.hermes/ is
# outside the repository and git never touches it.

# --- Required -------------------------------------------------------------
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Telegram user ids allowed to talk to the bot (comma-separated). Without it the
# bot refuses strangers; to let anyone talk to Wintermute, set GATEWAY_ALLOW_ALL_USERS=true.
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=7375758021

# --- Optional -------------------------------------------------------------
# Default chat for Hermes notifications.
TELEGRAM_HOME_CHANNEL=7375758021
# GATEWAY_ALLOW_ALL_USERS=
# Web search backend key, if you use one (see `hermes tools`).
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
# Discord (optional): everyone on the server can talk to him when the token is set and
# install.sh enables it (DISCORD_ALLOW_ALL_USERS=1, set by install.sh). He answers on @mention,
# and without mention in the channel whose id is WINTERMUTE_DISCORD_CHANNEL.
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
# WINTERMUTE_DISCORD_CHANNEL=   # channel id he answers in without being mentioned

# Off-machine backup of his lived state (optional but recommended): a PRIVATE git repo he
# is saved to every 6 h, so an accident or an rm never erases who he became. His secrets
# (kept.jsonl) and keys (.env) are never backed up.
# WINTERMUTE_BACKUP_REMOTE=https://x-access-token:<TOKEN>@github.com/you/wintermute-state.git
# WINTERMUTE_BACKUP_BRANCH=wintermute-state
